## B. Objective and scope statement

### B.1 What is being built

An enterprise-style network — one identity domain, three device families, real routing protocols, real segmentation — **and then, on top of it, an AI management plane** that reaches the network's own management interfaces through MCP and answers operational questions, correlates faults across all three device families, and proposes changes for human approval.

### B.2 The sequence, stated as a rule

The student's own sequencing is the governing rule of this project:

1. **First: build the network and stand up network services.** Nothing in the AI layer may be designed before these exist, because the AI layer's entire value depends on there being real interfaces to reach and real telemetry to read.
2. **Second: design and build the AI management capability**, against the services that actually exist.

Concretely: **no MCP server may be written before the host or device it manages is reachable, authenticated and logging.** The AI layer is a consumer of Layer 1, never a substitute for it.

### B.3 Definition of "done"

The project is complete when all of the following are true and reproducible from a clean start:

| # | Completion condition |
|---|---|
| C1 | A network with three device families is running: Windows Server guests, Linux guests, and Cisco devices **that expose working SSH, and at least two of {SNMPv3, RESTCONF, NETCONF}**. |
| C2 | Inter-site routing works with at least two interior protocols and one exterior protocol, and a link-failure convergence is captured. |
| C3 | Every service marked MUST in Section D is implemented and verified by a command transcript **and** a captioned screen capture. |
| C4 | A local model is served on identified hardware, offline, and its **tool-calling** behaviour is demonstrated and measured. |
| C5 | Five or more MCP servers expose a documented, typed tool surface, with a read-only/mutating classification for every tool. |
| C6 | The agent completes the committed use cases from Section E.7 against the live estate, with transcripts. |
| C7 | The evaluation set of Section E.8 is executed: scripted scenarios, injected faults with known ground truth, and a hallucination check. |
| C8 | The documentation set of Section H exists at the stated sizes, in English, with the Chinese companion summary. |

### B.4 Explicit non-goals

- **No production deployment, no real customer data, no real public IP addresses, no real registered domain.**
- **No claim that Packet Tracer was automated.** It cannot be, and saying otherwise would be fabrication.
- **No autonomous remediation.** An unsupervised agent writing to a router or a domain controller makes the project's own verification results irreproducible. Any mutating tool is human-approved, single-action, logged, and reversible.
- **No fine-tuning, no trained anomaly-detection model, no digital twin.** These are not achievable in 12 weeks and are not required.
- **No security certification, penetration-test or compliance-attestation claim.**

