## F. Phase and milestone plan (12 weeks, 4 people)

### F.1 The strict sequence, as gates

| Gate | Week | Condition to pass | If it fails |
|---|---|---|---|
| **G0 — Direction locked** | 1 | D-01 to D-05, D-09, D-11, D-12 answered; this outline signed off | Nothing else starts |
| **G1 — One Cisco device is genuinely reachable** | 3 | SSH login succeeds from the management host; `snmpwalk -v3` returns data; the exact `show version` string is captured | Fall back through the D-01 options immediately; do not spend week 4 hoping |
| **G2 — MUST core is up** | 6 | Every MUST row in Section D.1 verified with a transcript and a captioned screenshot | Cut SHOULD items; do **not** start the AI layer early to compensate |
| **G3 — AI feasibility closed** | 8 | A working local model calls a toy MCP tool reliably; the malformed-call rate is measured; D-06 and D-07 are confirmed or reduced | Reduce the committed use cases; never proceed on an unmeasured model |
| **G4 — Use cases demonstrated** | 10 | The committed use cases run end to end on the live estate | Drop to UC-1 and UC-5, and say so |
| **G5 — Evidence complete** | 11 | Evaluation set executed; drift baseline frozen; every screenshot captioned; every document at target size | Documentation slips into week 12 and the report becomes thin — this is the most likely failure mode |
| **G6 — Submission** | 12 | English report + Chinese companion assembled; consistency sweep clean; presentation rehearsed | — |

### F.2 Weekly plan

Roles: **S1 — Cisco/network**; **S2 — Identity & Windows**; **S3 — Linux & services/HA**; **S4 — Automation, monitoring, AI, documentation integrator**.

| Week | S1 (Cisco) | S2 (Windows) | S3 (Linux) | S4 (AI/Automation) | Gate / milestone |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Evaluate CML vs alternatives; get the platform installed on one machine | Build `W2K25-TEMPLATE-01`; confirm licence/media | Build `UBU2404-TEMPLATE-01`; host-only networks | Set up the Git repository, the evidence folder tree and the caption template | **G0** decisions signed off |
| 2 | Bring up the first device; VLANs and trunks in the design tool | AD DS forest, DNS, DHCP live | Baseline hardening; Nginx design | Ansible control node installed; inventory created | Templates done; host-only networks verified |
| 3 | **SSH + SNMPv3 working on one device — capture `show version`** | Two DCs replicating; OU tree and groups | Nginx + Keepalived live with a failover capture | First read-only collector script against the Linux estate | **G1** Cisco reachability |
| 4 | RSTP + inter-site OSPF on the Cisco layer | File server, FSRM quotas and screening | nftables chokepoint with logging | Prometheus + exporters + syslog receiver up | Routing between families works |
| 5 | ASA-class perimeter, ACLs, NAT | iSCSI target and initiator attached | Remote access chosen and built (OpenVPN **or** IKEv2) | **Local-model spike begins**: install the serving stack, test 3 candidate models for tool calling | Perimeter verified |
| 6 | HSRP/VRRP gateway redundancy | PKI issuing to the clients and web tier | DMZ published service through the proxy | **Local-model spike closes**; D-06/D-07 confirmed | **G2** MUST core complete |
